  "solution": {
    "text": "Expression $=\\left(1+x^{2}\\right)^{40} \\cdot\\left(x+\\frac{1}{x}\\right)^{-10}$\r\n$=\\left(1+x^{2}\\right)^{30} \\cdot x^{10}$\r\nThe coefficient of $x^{20}$ in $x^{10}\\left(1+x^{2}\\right)^{30}$ $=$ the coefficient of $\\mathrm{x}^{10}$ in $\\left(1+\\mathrm{x}^{2}\\right)^{30}$\r\n$={ }^{30} \\mathrm{C}_{5}={ }^{30} \\mathrm{C}_{30-5}={ }^{30} \\mathrm{C}_{25}$",
